{
  "id": "ss.char.cicada",
  "name": "Cicada",
  "description": "A survivor of the same brood as everything hunting you — same feelers, same organ, same socket in the shell. The organ is `dead`: no halo, no bloom, a hairline crack across cold grey, and that silence is the premise all eight wear in the same place. The hard two-plane facet, unchanged — and a pair of wings held spread behind it. The shell was already doing a cicada's job: a cicada at rest is two flat planes tented over its own back, which is what this diamond has always looked like, so the wings only finish the read. They are spread rather than folded because Chirp is a vibration and a folded wing does not read as one. The dead organ needs no moving: it already sits where a cicada's tymbal does, which makes the loudest insect there is the one carrying the broken voice.",
